{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Coincidences", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Let Me Tell You a Story", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Writing a Short Narrative", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br/><br/>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience.<br/><br/>When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To help you decide whether you should use the Present Perfect tense or the Past Simple tense, ask yourself the questions \u2018When?'", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you can answer the question \u2018When?', then the past time is stated or inferred or understood. There is no connection to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the you cannot answer the question \u2018When?', then the time is not stated or not important and you would choose the Present Perfect tense because there is a connection to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I have never shared this story with anyone. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It has shaken me and left me with nightmares. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I stumbled to my feet, glanced at the moon and scurried home.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I sat on a park bench near the lake shore and contemplated the beauty of nature.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to shake", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause someone to feel fear, anxiety and shock", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It has shaken me and left me with nightmares. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in a narrative about a strange event.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pub", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small restaurant, typical to Great Britain or Ireland, where you can buy drinks and order meals", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  A party had been organized by my friends at a local pub but I had arrived too late. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to contemplate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think deeply or carefully about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I sat on a park bench near the lake shore and contemplated the beauty of nature. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "disoriented", "type": "name"}, {"content": "lost or confused", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I rubbed my eyes to wake up but felt disoriented.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "paralyzed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unable to do anything out of fear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was paralyzed by the shocking sight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "menacing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "dangerous or possibly harmful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The menacing, faceless animal moved closer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to latch on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to grab and hold", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It started to extend his arms to latch onto my legs.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to scurry", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move quickly and with short steps", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I stumbled to my feet, glanced at the moon and scurried home.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Talk to your friends and family about a strange event or coincidence they have experienced.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes based on the conversation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now, write a 150-170 word short narrative based on the notes you gathered.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You will need to include: <ul><li>A narrator - the person or \u201cvoice\u201d telling the story to a reader</li><li>A setting - specific time and place the story is set</li> <li>Characters - the people or animals in a story</li> <li> A plot -  a series of events that happen in the story - What happens?</li><li>A solution - the end of the plot, how the story finishes</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use both the Past tense and Present Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your narrative aloud to your friend or family member.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss a strange event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes based on conversations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a short narrative about a strange event.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can write about coincidences and strange events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write a short narrative.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write about past events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How often do you read short stories? What kind?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you prefer true stories or fictional stories? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Writing Spot: Don't get too close to the river ...", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"_data": [{"typ